# OPTIONAL: one wildcard certificate for every tenant sub-domain (*.BASE) instead of one
# on-demand certificate per centre. Recommended once you expect more new centres per week
# than your CA's "new certificates per registered domain" limit allows.
#
# A wildcard certificate can only be obtained with the ACME DNS-01 challenge, so:
#   1. build Caddy with the module of YOUR DNS provider (infrastructure/docker/caddy/Dockerfile,
#      build arg CADDY_DNS_MODULE, list: https://github.com/caddy-dns);
#   2. give Caddy an API token that may edit TXT records of the zone (caddy.env: CADDY_DNS_API_TOKEN);
#   3. copy this file to sites/wildcard.caddy and adapt the `dns` line to your provider's syntax;
#   4. create the DNS record  *.BASE  A/AAAA  -> this server.
#
# Explicit hosts (api., app., admin., corporate., portal.) keep their own sites: Caddy always
# prefers the most specific host name. Verified CUSTOM domains keep using on-demand TLS
# through the catch-all site of Caddyfile.prod.
#
# The example uses Cloudflare. Not exercised in the authoring workspace.
*.{$TYPEASE_BASE_DOMAIN} {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CADDY_DNS_API_TOKEN}
	}
	import security_headers
	import access_log
	encode zstd gzip
	request_body {
		max_size {$UPLOAD_MAX_BODY:16MB}
	}
	import web_routes customer-web 3002
}
